  "id": "COMPOUND:43464 - PROTEIN:5794",
  "verbalization": "Alloocimene, (4Z,6Z)- is consistently identified as a target of LAPC4 through multiple pathways, with the intermediate entities Carboxylesterase 2 and 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One acting as mediators. These intermediates are linked to LAPC4 via a series of target relationships, suggesting a potential mechanism where Alloocimene, (4Z,6,Z)- influences the activity of these enzymes, which in turn modulate LAPC4. The shared involvement of Carboxylesterase 2 in both pathways highlights a possible common pathway or a redundant mechanism, while the distinct intermediates in Path 1 and Path 2 indicate that Alloocimene, (4Z,6,Z)- may act through different routes to affect LAPC4. The evidence supports a role for Alloocimene, (4Z,6,Z)- in the regulation of LAPC4 through enzymatic interactions, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
